[stderr] # 06 — Foundation and domain authoring contracts
[stderr] 
[stderr] **Inputs:** [delivery map](05-delivery-map.md), [technical contract](../specification/03-technical-contract.md), [feature model](../specification/02-feature-model.md), and [experience contract](../specification/04-experience-contract.md).
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Purpose and use
[stderr] 
[stderr] This is the authoring input for later implementation runbooks. Each record is
[stderr] an atomic, independently reviewable outcome; it is not authority to choose an
[stderr] engine, vendor, remote service, or production browser matrix. A later runbook
[stderr] must name its contract ID, preserve its ownership boundary, and either resolve
[stderr] the listed decision gate or stop before work that depends on it.
[stderr] 
[stderr] The P0 product remains a client-side, offline, single-player web/PWA campaign.
[stderr] `Shared` denotes work used by both responsive web and installed PWA. `Web`
[stderr] denotes browser-only work; `PWA` denotes a service-worker/install adaptation.
[stderr] No contract below creates account, sync, multiplayer, commerce, analytics, or
[stderr] live-service functionality.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Contract record conventions
[stderr] 
[stderr] - **Implementation ID** is stable and must be cited by dependent runbooks.
[stderr] - **Owns** gives the sole initial owner of files and durable data. Paths are
[stderr]   planned paths until FDN-01 has an approved framework.
[stderr] - **Does not own** prevents adjacent work from being pulled forward.
[stderr] - **Acceptance evidence** is the artifact a supervisor can inspect after the
[stderr]   stated verification passes.
[stderr] - A decision gate is a blocking approval, not a default that an author may
[stderr]   silently select.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Foundation contracts
[stderr] 
[stderr] ### FDN-01 — Bootstrap the reproducible project baseline
[stderr] 
[stderr] - **Scope / target:** Shared build and test baseline for responsive web and
[stderr]   PWA; no gameplay or PWA cache implementation.
[stderr] - **Bounded outcome:** An approved engine/framework project skeleton has one
[stderr]   documented bootstrap command, deterministic test command, lint/format
[stderr]   commands, and the planned source/test directory boundaries.
[stderr] - **Dependencies:** Approved engine/framework, package manager, and CI runtime.
[stderr] - **Owns:** Root build/tooling configuration; `src/{core,content,platform/web,app}/`;
[stderr]   `tests/{core,content,platform,app}/`; `docs/development.md`.
[stderr] - **Does not own:** Domain rules, content, persistence implementation, UI,
[stderr]   service worker, hosting, or a browser support promise.
[stderr] - **Verification:** Clean checkout/bootstrap succeeds in the approved runtime;
[stderr]   formatting and lint commands pass; a deterministic core sample test runs.
[stderr] - **Acceptance evidence:** Pinned toolchain/version declaration, documented
[stderr]   command transcript, and CI-equivalent check output.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ### FDN-02 — Declare configuration and environment boundaries
[stderr] 
[stderr] - **Scope / target:** Shared release configuration with Web/PWA build inputs;
[stderr]   no remote runtime configuration or secrets.
[stderr] - **Bounded outcome:** Typed, validated build configuration separates public
[stderr]   release metadata from development-only settings, fails closed for absent or
[stderr]   malformed required values, and prevents client-secret inclusion.
[stderr] - **Dependencies:** FDN-01; approved release/versioning and hosting inputs.
[stderr] - **Owns:** Root configuration schema/loader; checked-in example configuration;
[stderr]   build-time environment documentation; release metadata interface.
[stderr] - **Does not own:** Account credentials, telemetry endpoints, feature flags for
[stderr]   unapproved services, or values for undecided vendors/hosts.
[stderr] - **Verification:** Valid sample configuration builds; missing/invalid required
[stderr]   value fails with actionable output; release artifact scan finds no secret-like
[stderr]   configured value.
[stderr] - **Acceptance evidence:** Configuration contract, sample file, negative-test
[stderr]   fixtures, and an artifact-scan report.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ### FDN-03 — Establish architecture seams and dependency rules
[stderr] 
[stderr] - **Scope / target:** Shared core/content/application boundaries plus Web and
[stderr]   PWA adapter boundaries.
[stderr] - **Bounded outcome:** Enforced imports/interfaces ensure the deterministic
[stderr]   core has no browser, renderer, timer, or network dependency; UI and input
[stderr]   submit commands only; persistence serializes confirmed core state only.
[stderr] - **Dependencies:** FDN-01; FDN-02 for build-time enforcement configuration.
[stderr] - **Owns:** `src/core/` public command/state/event interfaces; boundary/lint
[stderr]   rules; adapter interface definitions; architecture decision documentation.
[stderr] - **Does not own:** Concrete combat, exploration, UI panels, storage driver,
[stderr]   service worker, or content package data.
[stderr] - **Verification:** Dependency-rule test rejects forbidden core imports; a
[stderr]   fixture adapter can submit an action and render returned state/events without
[stderr]   direct state mutation.
[stderr] - **Acceptance evidence:** Dependency graph/check output, public-interface
[stderr]   inventory, and passing adapter fixture test.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ### FDN-04 — Define semantic design-token contracts
[stderr] 
[stderr] - **Scope / target:** Shared visual/accessibility semantics, with responsive
[stderr]   Web layout use and PWA inheriting the same tokens.
[stderr] - **Bounded outcome:** Original, named tokens cover restrained warm-fantasy
[stderr]   colour roles, typography scale, spacing, radii, elevation, focus, motion,
[stderr]   touch target, status, and non-colour state cues; tokens support text scaling,
[stderr]   contrast modes, reduced motion, and captions without asserting final art.
[stderr] - **Dependencies:** FDN-01; accessibility acceptance criteria; final font and
[stderr]   contrast targets remain approval gates.
[stderr] - **Owns:** `src/app/design/tokens/`; token documentation; token validation or
[stderr]   preview fixtures.
[stderr] - **Does not own:** Screens, maps, copied reference styling, art/audio assets,
[stderr]   final responsive breakpoints, or gameplay UI implementation.
[stderr] - **Verification:** Token build/type validation passes; sample semantic states
[stderr]   retain a text label and non-colour cue; reduced-motion values remove or bound
[stderr]   non-essential animation.
[stderr] - **Acceptance evidence:** Token inventory with role rationale, original-style
[stderr]   provenance note, and automated validation/sample capture.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ### FDN-05 — Model deterministic campaign data and commands
[stderr] 
[stderr] - **Scope / target:** Shared, browser-free domain model for both delivery
[stderr]   surfaces.
[stderr] - **Bounded outcome:** Immutable campaign state, typed commands/results/events,
[stderr]   revisions, interaction IDs, deterministic RNG state, and invariant helpers
[stderr]   define legal transitions without implementing later feature state machines.
[stderr] - **Dependencies:** FDN-01 and FDN-03; party size and content quantities are
[stderr]   approval gates for any concrete shape beyond the minimum contract.
[stderr] - **Owns:** `src/core/{state,commands,events,invariants,rng}/` and
[stderr]   `tests/core/contract.*`.
[stderr] - **Does not own:** Authored content values, inventory/combat/quest algorithms,
[stderr]   save storage, UI selection state, account profiles, or network state.
[stderr] - **Verification:** Unit tests show invalid commands do not mutate state,
[stderr]   expected-revision mismatch rejects stale intent, and repeated interaction IDs
[stderr]   do not produce an extra durable transition.
[stderr] - **Acceptance evidence:** Versioned type/interface reference, invariant-test
[stderr]   report, and rejection/idempotency fixtures.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ### FDN-06 — Define the local persistence and recovery protocol
[stderr] 
[stderr] - **Scope / target:** Shared save schema/protocol with a Web local-storage
[stderr]   adapter; installed PWA uses the same browser-origin data independently of
[stderr]   cache lifecycle.
[stderr] - **Bounded outcome:** A schema contract specifies immutable revisions,
[stderr]   checksums, validated current pointer, last-known-good retention, quarantine,
[stderr]   settings separation, deletion confirmation, and pure ordered migrations.
[stderr] - **Dependencies:** FDN-03 and FDN-05; approved browser storage API/quota and
[stderr]   save-support retention policy.
[stderr] - **Owns:** `src/core/save/{schema,compatibility,migrations}/`;
[stderr]   `src/platform/web/persistence/`; `tests/{core,platform}/**/*save*`; save and
[stderr]   recovery documentation.
[stderr] - **Does not own:** Cloud sync, account-linked saves, content import/export,
[stderr]   PWA cache records, or a guarantee after user/browser storage eviction.
[stderr] - **Verification:** Fault-injection fixtures cover interrupted write, checksum
[stderr]   failure, malformed/unsupported migration, quota/permission failure,
[stderr]   quarantine, retry, and selected-slot deletion; every supported predecessor
[stderr]   fixture migrates once without modifying its original bytes.
[stderr] - **Acceptance evidence:** Save-state diagram, schema compatibility table,
[stderr]   fixtures, and passing fault/migration report showing retained valid revision.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ### FDN-07 — Bound the deferred identity contract
[stderr] 
[stderr] - **Scope / target:** Explicit P0 exclusion shared by Web and PWA; no identity
[stderr]   adapter is built.
[stderr] - **Bounded outcome:** The domain and storage interfaces prove no player
[stderr]   account identifier, authentication token, remote profile, or sync authority
[stderr]   is needed for an offline campaign; future identity integration requirements
[stderr]   are recorded as a decision gate.
[stderr] - **Dependencies:** FDN-03, FDN-05; explicit product/privacy/security/vendor
[stderr]   approval before any connected identity work.
[stderr] - **Owns:** Architecture/privacy decision record and contract tests asserting
[stderr]   local-save interfaces require only local slot identity.
[stderr] - **Does not own:** Sign-up, sign-in, guest accounts, OAuth, session handling,
[stderr]   cloud sync, remote deletion, or support identity lookups.
[stderr] - **Verification:** Static/dependency scan finds no account/token fields or
[stderr]   network identity client in P0 foundation modules; local campaign start/save/
[stderr]   resume fixture runs with no identity input.
[stderr] - **Acceptance evidence:** Recorded P0 exclusion, future-approval checklist
[stderr]   (identity provider, consent, outage, retention/deletion, support, conflict),
[stderr]   and scan/test output.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ### FDN-08 — Bound the deferred authorization contract
[stderr] 
[stderr] - **Scope / target:** Explicit P0 exclusion shared by Web and PWA; browser
[stderr]   profile control is not presented as authorization.
[stderr] - **Bounded outcome:** The contracts state that P0 has no server resource or
[stderr]   role boundary; future authorization must be server-enforced, least-privilege,
[stderr]   authenticated per request, auditable, rate-limited, and resilient to outage.
[stderr] - **Dependencies:** FDN-07 and explicit approval for a server resource and
[stderr]   identity policy.
[stderr] - **Owns:** Security/architecture decision record and negative contract tests
[stderr]   that domain commands do not accept client-asserted role/permission fields.
[stderr] - **Does not own:** Roles, permissions, administration, moderation, player
[stderr]   safety, purchase entitlement, server APIs, or client-side permission checks.
[stderr] - **Verification:** Type/interface scan confirms no authorization fields in
[stderr]   P0 commands/snapshots; negative fixture rejects or cannot construct a
[stderr]   client-supplied privilege claim.
[stderr] - **Acceptance evidence:** P0 authorization-exclusion statement, future
[stderr]   service authorization checklist, and passing negative test/scan report.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ### FDN-09 — Build the layered deterministic test harness
[stderr] 
[stderr] - **Scope / target:** Shared unit/content/integration harness; Web adapter
[stderr]   checks; PWA lifecycle browser tests only after service-worker work exists.
[stderr] - **Bounded outcome:** Test conventions and fixtures make deterministic domain,
[stderr]   content validation, persistence fault injection, application integration,
[stderr]   and browser-change coverage independently runnable with isolated data and no
[stderr]   real services.
[stderr] - **Dependencies:** FDN-01–FDN-06; FDN-07–FDN-08 exclusion fixtures; approved
[stderr]   browser/device matrix and performance budgets for final target claims.
[stderr] - **Owns:** Test-runner configuration; fixture factories; deterministic RNG/
[stderr]   clock controls; `tests/{core,content,platform,app}/`; test guidance; reserved
[stderr]   `supervisor/browser/tests/changes/` conventions.
[stderr] - **Does not own:** Final game feature assertions, production telemetry,
[stderr]   performance-budget values, or a smoke spec before a browser-facing feature
[stderr]   has an implemented surface.
[stderr] - **Verification:** One command runs each test layer; a deliberately failing
[stderr]   fixture is detected; fixtures cannot write to a real player slot; repeated
[stderr]   run produces identical core result/event data.
[stderr] - **Acceptance evidence:** Test command matrix, fixture-isolation proof,
[stderr]   deterministic-run comparison, and documented mapping from later contract IDs
[stderr]   to their unit/integration/browser evidence.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Authoring order and cross-target allocation
[stderr] 
[stderr] | Order | Contract | Later runbook may start when | Target allocation |
[stderr] | --- | --- | --- | --- |
[stderr] | 1 | FDN-01 | Framework/toolchain approval exists. | Shared baseline |
[stderr] | 2 | FDN-02, FDN-03 | FDN-01 is verified. | Shared; Web/PWA build boundaries |
[stderr] | 3 | FDN-04, FDN-05 | Architecture seams are verified. | Shared; Web token consumption |
[stderr] | 4 | FDN-06, FDN-09 | Core contract and storage decision are approved. | Shared schema, Web adapter, PWA inherits saves |
[stderr] | Gate only | FDN-07, FDN-08 | A connected product decision is explicitly approved. | No P0 implementation on either target |
