 |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/traceability-matrix.md:11:| REQ-0006, NFR-0002\u20130003 | J5 | save/session/recovery; FDN-06, FEX-10,11, QOR-04 | DM-05,06,07,12; IMP unassigned | atomic/fault/migration/quarantine tests |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/traceability-matrix.md:12:| REQ-0007, NFR-0004\u20130005 | J1,J6 | shell/input/settings/a11y; FDN-04, FEX-06\u201309 | DM-13,15,16; IMP unassigned | accessibility scans, focused browser/manual evidence |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/traceability-matrix.md:13:| REQ-0009\u20130010, NFR-0010 | J1,J6 | responsive shell/input adapters; FDN-03, FEX-06,07 | DM-13,15,16; IMP unassigned | input unit + responsive browser matrix |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/traceability-matrix.md:14:| REQ-0011, NFR-0001, NFR-0011 | J7 | PWA/cache/release; FEX-12,14, QOR-04\u201305,08 | DM-17\u201320; IMP unassigned | offline/update/cache/rollback evidence |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/traceability-matrix.md:15:| REQ-0012, NFR-0006 | J5,J7 | recovery/diagnostics; FDN-06, FEX-11, QOR-02\u201304 | DM-07,12,18\u201320; IMP unassigned | injected-error, consent/redaction evidence |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/traceability-matrix.md:16:| NFR-0007 | J2\u2013J5 | content validator; FDN-05, FEX-13 | DM-03,04; IMP unassigned | invalid-reference/reachability suite |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/traceability-matrix.md:17:| NFR-0008 | J1\u2013J7 | content/assets/release; FEX-09,13, QOR-06 | DM-04,18,20; IMP unassigned | provenance manifest + human review |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/traceability-matrix.md:18:| NFR-0009, NFR-0012 | J1,J7 | quality/release controls; FDN-01\u201303, QOR-01,05\u201308 | DM-01,18\u201320; IMP unassigned | approved-matrix reports, gate records |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/traceability-matrix.md:19:| REQ-0013\u20130015 | none (not P0) | exclusion seams; FDN-07,08, QOR-01 | no P0 runbook; IMP unassigned | decision/gate audit; approved future contract only |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/05-delivery-map.md:5:## Purpose and ordering\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/05-delivery-map.md:19:### Planned implementation layout\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/05-delivery-map.md:32:## Shared foundations\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/05-delivery-map.md:36:| DM-01 | Create the selected-framework project skeleton, deterministic test runner, lint/format commands, and the source/test directories above. | Approval of engine/framework | Root build/config files; `src/`; `tests/`; `docs/development.md` | Clean bootstrap; lint/format; one deterministic sample-core test. |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/05-delivery-map.md:37:| DM-02 | Define immutable domain state, typed commands/results/events, revisions, interaction IDs, deterministic RNG state, and invariant helpers with no browser imports. | DM-01 | `src/core/{state,commands,events,invariants,rng}`; `tests/core/contract.*` | Unit tests prove command rejection is non-mutating and expected-revision checks reject stale requests. |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/05-delivery-map.md:38:| DM-03 | Implement the versioned content-package types and build-time validator for IDs, references, localisation, asset manifest, quest predicates, rewards, and campaign reachability. | DM-01, DM-02; content-format approval | `src/content/{schema,validator,registry}`; `content/`; `tests/content/validation.*` | Valid-minimum package passes; one fixture per invalid reference class fails; graph test proves opening-to-ending reachability. |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/05-delivery-map.md:39:| DM-04 | Author the original minimal Larkspur Reach / Glassroot Hollow content package: town, dungeon, dialogue, tutorial, quests, encounters, items, rewards, ending, base locale, and provenance records. | DM-03; content quantities/party-size approval | `content/base/`; `assets/source-manifest.*`; `docs/content-authoring.md` | Content validation passes; review confirms original provenance and one complete campaign path. |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/05-delivery-map.md:40:| DM-05 | Implement atomic local snapshot repository: checksummed immutable revisions, current pointer, last-known-good retention, quarantine, delete semantics, and separately persisted preferences. | DM-02; storage-API/quota approval | `src/platform/web/persistence/`; `src/core/save/`; `tests/platform/persistence.*` | Fault-injection tests cover interrupted write, malformed snapshot, quota/permission failure, quarantine, and selected-slot deletion. |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/05-delivery-map.md:41:| DM-06 | Implement save schema compatibility declarations and pure, ordered migration runner that promotes only validated candidates. | DM-03, DM-05 | `src/core/save/{schema,migrations,compatibility}`; migration fixtures in `tests/core/save/` | Every supported predecessor fixture migrates once; failed/unsupported migration preserves original quarantine data. |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/05-delivery-map.md:42:| DM-07 | Establish error boundary, player recovery model, bounded local diagnostic record, consent/clear controls, and no-network guardrails. | DM-01, DM-05 | `src/app/recovery/`; `src/platform/web/diagnostics/`; `docs/privacy-and-recovery.md`; `tests/app/recovery.*` | Tests show retry/title/safe-recovery keep confirmed progress; diagnostics are absent without consent and exclude save/dialogue payloads. |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/05-delivery-map.md:44:## Domain and campaign features\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/05-delivery-map.md:48:| DM-08 | Implement quest, dialogue, campaign, and tutorial state machines, including idempotent objective/reward/checkpoint ordering and ending completion. | DM-02, DM-03, DM-04, DM-05 | `src/core/{quest,dialogue,campaign,tutorial}`; `tests/core/campaign.*` | Tests cover repeated interaction, locked predicates, one-time rewards, tutorial progression, and ending transition. |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/05-delivery-map.md:49:| DM-09 | Implement party, legal turn-based encounter resolution, visible turn events, defeat-to-checkpoint rule, and deterministic combat fixtures. | DM-02, DM-03, DM-05, DM-08 | `src/core/combat/`; `tests/core/combat.*` | Tests reject stale/illegal action or target without consuming a turn; deterministic win/loss and reward-once fixtures pass. |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/05-delivery-map.md:50:| DM-10 | Implement inventory and authored party progression mutations: acquire, inspect, use/equip eligibility, quest-item protection, and duplicate-grant ledger behaviour. | DM-02, DM-03, DM-08, DM-09 | `src/core/{inventory,party,rewards}`; `tests/core/inventory.*` | Tests cover empty inventory, illegal use, protected quest items, ineligible targets, and duplicate grant rejection. |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/05-delivery-map.md:51:| DM-11 | Implement scene exploration rules for collision, interactions, exits, encounter zones, and safe scene boundaries across exactly one town and one dungeon. | DM-02, DM-03, DM-04, DM-08, DM-09 | `src/core/exploration/`; `tests/core/exploration.*` | Scripted route traverses town to dungeon to ending; locked exit and missing/invalid content states fail safely. |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/05-delivery-map.md:52:| DM-12 | Integrate core commands with the save/checkpoint coordinator so manual saves, authored checkpoints, rewards, scene exits, and recovery obey one safe-boundary policy. | DM-05, DM-06, DM-08\u2013DM-11 | `src/core/session/`; `src/app/session/`; `tests/{core,app}/checkpoint.*` | Integration tests prove no unresolved combat is persisted, prior confirmed snapshot survives failed save, and resume restores a safe scene. |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/05-delivery-map.md:54:## Web adapters, UI, input, and accessibility\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/05-delivery-map.md:58:| DM-13 | Build the responsive semantic application shell: title/new/continue/load navigation, pause/focus/visibility behaviour, game stage, panels, status messages, and error-boundary entry points. | DM-01, DM-07, DM-12 | `src/app/{shell,navigation,status}`; `tests/app/shell.*`; `supervisor/browser/tests/changes/dm-13-shell-navigation.spec.*` | App integration tests; Playwright covers no-save title state, panel return target, focus-loss pause, and phone/tablet/desktop shell reflow. |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/05-delivery-map.md:59:| DM-14 | Deliver exploration, dialogue, quest, party, inventory, combat, and ending presentation bound only to core state/events, with readable empty/locked/invalid feedback. | DM-04, DM-08\u2013DM-13 | `src/app/{game,panels,combat,dialogue}`; `tests/app/gameplay-ui.*`; `supervisor/browser/tests/changes/dm-14-gameplay-ui.spec.*` | State-driven UI tests; Playwright completes the tutorial battle and verifies empty inventory, locked exit, visible objective, and ending path. |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/05-delivery-map.md:60:| DM-15 | Implement web input adapters for keyboard, mouse, touch, and feature-detected gamepad, all mapping to one action vocabulary with focus-safe repeat/debounce handling. | DM-02, DM-13 | `src/platform/web/input/`; `src/app/controls/`; `tests/platform/input.*`; `supervisor/browser/tests/changes/dm-15-input-adapters.spec.*` | Unit tests map each adapter to semantic actions; Playwright validates keyboard-only navigation, touch targets, pointer equivalence, and unavailable-gamepad fallback. |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/05-delivery-map.md:61:| DM-16 | Implement settings and accessibility adaptations: text/spacing, contrast/non-colour cues, captions, audio, reduced motion, on-screen controls, locale fallback, semantic landmarks, accessible names, dialogs, and focus restoration. | DM-05, DM-13\u2013DM-15; language/control-remapping/audio approvals as applicable | `src/app/{settings,accessibility,i18n}`; `tests/app/accessibility.*`; `supervisor/browser/tests/changes/dm-16-accessibility-settings.spec.*` | Automated accessibility scan plus keyboard/focus assertions; Playwright verifies settings persistence failure notice, 200% text/reflow, reduced motion, dialog Cancel default, and captions/contrast settings. |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/05-delivery-map.md:63:## Distribution, trust, operations, documentation, QA, and release\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/05-delivery-map.md:67:| DM-17 | Add PWA manifest, install affordance, asset manifest/precache, offline status, known-good cache retention, and safe-boundary update activation independent from saves. | DM-04\u2013DM-07, DM-12\u2013DM-16; service-worker rollout approval | `public/{manifest,icons}`; `src/platform/web/pwa/`; service-worker/build config; `tests/platform/pwa.*`; `supervisor/browser/tests/changes/dm-17-pwa-lifecycle.spec.*` | Browser test covers uncached offline explanation, cached offline reload, declined/unavailable install, refresh failure retention, and update deferred until title/pause after confirmed save. |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/05-delivery-map.md:68:| DM-18 | Add release hardening: build asset hashes, CSP/static-host headers, dependency/license/provenance review, parser/size bounds, and client secret scan. | DM-01, DM-03, DM-04, DM-17; hosting approval | Build/host config; `scripts/release-check.*`; `docs/security-and-provenance.md`; `tests/security/` | Release check verifies hashed manifest, CSP/header policy, no secret findings, dependency/provenance inventory, and hostile content/save payload rejection. |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/05-delivery-map.md:69:| DM-19 | Define and automate quality evidence: core/content/persistence integration suite, target-browser matrix runner, responsive/accessibility manual checklist, offline/storage cases, and approval-gated performance measurement. | DM-01\u2013DM-18; browser/device/budget approval | Test configuration; `docs/quality-plan.md`; `docs/test-matrix.md`; `supervisor/browser/tests/changes/dm-19-release-evidence.spec.*` | CI-equivalent local suite is green; Playwright smoke verifies primary start/save/resume path; documented manual matrix has evidence fields and clearly marks unapproved targets/budgets. |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/05-delivery-map.md:70:| DM-20 | Produce player and operator release material: controls/help, save/recovery and privacy guidance, accessibility statement, support/version/cache status, content authoring/release checklist, rollback procedure, and release compatibility declaration. | DM-04\u2013DM-19 | `docs/{player-guide,accessibility,privacy-and-recovery,release-runbook,rollback,content-authoring}.md`; in-app Help/Status copy | Documentation review against contracts; dry-run release/rollback using a known-good build without changing player saves. |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/05-delivery-map.md:72:## Dependency summary\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/05-delivery-map.md:82:## Explicitly excluded or approval-gated work\n\ncodex\n{\"status\":\"pass\",\"summary\":\"The canonical material already separates P0 from held connected services and defines a DM-01\u201320 dependency order. I\u2019m using \u201cfoundation and core contracts\u201d as the first bounded shard; campaign, UI/input/accessibility, PWA/release, and held connected scope remain explicit queued shards.\",\"changed_files\":[],\"test_result\":\"\",\"evidence\":{\"agent_log\":\"Canonical specification and planning documents inspected.\",\"adapter_log\":\"\",\"test_log\":\"\",\"browser_log\":\"\",\"screenshots\":[]},\"acceptance_results\":[],\"documentation\":{\"reviewed_files\":[\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/README.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/requirements.json\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/05-delivery-map.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/06-foundation-domain-contracts.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/07-feature-experience-contracts.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/08-quality-operations-contracts.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/10-authoring-handoff.md\"],\"updated_files\":[],\"summary\":\"Planning inputs establish the bounded domain, ownership, gates, and traceability source.\"},\"known_limitations\":[],\"browser_coverage\":\"\",\"recommended_next_step\":\"complete\"}\napply patch\npatch: completed\n/Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json\n/Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.md\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..7f4cf1bcf472afd1c38d8fac9f5522e6a6b41be2\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json\n@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@\n+{\n+  \"catalogue_id\": \"mock-fantasy-quest-4-implementation-catalogue\",\n+  \"version\": 1,\n+  \"source\": [\"../specification/README.md\", \"../specification/requirements.json\", \"05-delivery-map.md\", \"06-foundation-domain-contracts.md\", \"07-feature-experience-contracts.md\", \"08-quality-operations-contracts.md\"],\n+  \"scope\": \"P0 is an original, offline-capable 2D single-player fantasy RPG delivered through a shared web core and a PWA delivery adaptation. Connected services are not P0 implementation scope.\",\n+  \"first_bounded_domain\": {\"id\": \"SHARD-01\", \"title\": \"Foundation and core contracts\", \"contract_limit\": 250, \"contract_count\": 12, \"state\": \"ready_for_authoring\", \"boundary\": \"Framework-neutral seams, deterministic state/data contracts, local persistence protocol, quality foundations, and original-design controls; excludes campaign rules, UI flows, PWA lifecycle, and release execution.\"},\n+  \"contracts\": [\n+    {\"id\":\"IMP-0001\",\"title\":\"Bootstrap reproducible shared project baseline\",\"domain\":\"foundation\",\"targets\":[\"shared\",\"web\",\"pwa\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"NFR-0010\",\"NFR-0012\"],\"bounded_outcome\":\"A framework-neutral project skeleton documents one bootstrap, lint, format, and deterministic test command with isolated shared, web-adapter, PWA-adapter, content, and test directories.\",\"prerequisites\":[],\"ownership\":{\"files\":[\"root build/tooling configuration\",\"src/{core,content,app,platform/web,platform/pwa}/\",\"tests/\",\"docs/development.md\"],\"data\":[\"pinned toolchain declaration\"],\"api\":[\"build/test command interface\"]},\"forbidden_scope\":[\"selecting framework/package manager/CI without DEC-0001\",\"gameplay\",\"service worker\",\"hosting\"],\"verification\":\"Clean approved-runtime checkout runs the documented deterministic sample test, lint, and format checks.\",\"human_external_gate\":\"GATE-0001 / DEC-0001 framework, package-manager, and CI selection before implementation.\",\"complexity\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"gated\"},\n+    {\"id\":\"IMP-0002\",\"title\":\"Enforce shared-core and adapter dependency seams\",\"domain\":\"foundation\",\"targets\":[\"shared\",\"web\",\"pwa\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"NFR-0010\",\"REQ-0013\",\"NFR-0012\"],\"bounded_outcome\":\"A dependency policy and public interfaces prevent core code from importing browser, renderer, clock, network, or platform modules; adapters submit commands and render returned state/events.\",\"prerequisites\":[\"IMP-0001\"],\"ownership\":{\"files\":[\"src/core/public interfaces\",\"src/platform/{web,pwa}/adapter interfaces\",\"architecture dependency rules\",\"docs/architecture.md\"],\"data\":[\"dependency-policy manifest\"],\"api\":[\"Command, state, event, and adapter interfaces\"]},\"forbidden_scope\":[\"concrete combat/exploration/UI\",\"account or network client\",\"target-specific campaign rules\"],\"verification\":\"A dependency-rule test rejects forbidden core imports and a fixture adapter proves command-only interaction.\",\"human_external_gate\":\"None; retain GATE-0001 for tool-specific enforcement.\",\"complexity\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"current\"},\n+    {\"id\":\"IMP-0003\",\"title\":\"Create deterministic test and fixture harness\",\"domain\":\"tests\",\"targets\":[\"shared\",\"web\",\"pwa\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"NFR-0010\",\"NFR-0012\"],\"bounded_outcome\":\"Layered unit, content, integration, and reserved browser-test conventions provide isolated RNG/clock and persistence fixtures with no real service or player data access.\",\"prerequisites\":[\"IMP-0001\",\"IMP-0002\"],\"ownership\":{\"files\":[\"test-runner configuration\",\"tests/{core,content,platform,app}/fixtures\",\"docs/testing.md\"],\"data\":[\"deterministic fixture factories\"],\"api\":[\"test fixture and fake clock/RNG interfaces\"]},\"forbidden_scope\":[\"final feature assertions\",\"real browser/device matrix claims\",\"production telemetry\"],\"verification\":\"Repeated core fixture execution has identical results; a deliberately failing fixture is detected; fixture storage is isolated.\",\"human_external_gate\":\"GATE-0002 before compatibility or performance claims.\",\"complexity\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"current\"},\n+    {\"id\":\"IMP-0004\",\"title\":\"Define deterministic campaign state and command contract\",\"domain\":\"data\",\"targets\":[\"shared\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"REQ-0001\",\"REQ-0003\",\"REQ-0004\",\"REQ-0006\",\"NFR-0002\",\"NFR-0010\"],\"bounded_outcome\":\"Immutable versioned state, command/result/event envelopes, revision and interaction identifiers, deterministic RNG state, and invariant helpers define legal transition mechanics without feature state machines.\",\"prerequisites\":[\"IMP-0002\",\"IMP-0003\"],\"ownership\":{\"files\":[\"src/core/{state,commands,events,invariants,rng}/\",\"tests/core/contract.*\"],\"data\":[\"campaign snapshot envelope\",\"deterministic RNG state\"],\"api\":[\"Core command/state/event API\"]},\"forbidden_scope\":[\"authored values\",\"combat/inventory/quest algorithms\",\"save driver\",\"UI selection state\",\"account/network state\"],\"verification\":\"Invalid and stale commands do not mutate state; duplicate interaction IDs cause no extra durable transition.\",\"human_external_gate\":\"GATE-0004 before concrete party/content shapes.\",\"complexity\":\"high\",\"status\":\"current\"},\n+    {\"id\":\"IMP-0005\",\"title\":\"Define versioned content schema and validation boundary\",\"domain\":\"content\",\"targets\":[\"shared\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"REQ-0002\",\"REQ-0008\",\"NFR-0007\",\"NFR-0008\"],\"bounded_outcome\":\"Typed content-package schema and validator cover IDs, references, locale keys, assets, predicates, rewards, and reachability but contain no authored campaign expression.\",\"prerequisites\":[\"IMP-0001\",\"IMP-0004\",\"IMP-0003\"],\"ownership\":{\"files\":[\"src/content/{schema,validator,registry}/\",\"tests/content/validation.*\",\"docs/content-authoring.md\"],\"data\":[\"versioned content package format\",\"asset/provenance manifest schema\"],\"api\":[\"content registry and validator API\"]},\"forbidden_scope\":[\"town/dungeon dialogue/maps/assets\",\"copied reference expression\",\"release packaging\"],\"verification\":\"Valid minimum package passes; each invalid reference class fails; a graph fixture checks opening-to-ending reachability.\",\"human_external_gate\":\"GATE-0004 for quantities, locale, and content detail; human provenance review remains required.\",\"complexity\":\"high\",\"status\":\"current\"},\n+    {\"id\":\"IMP-0006\",\"title\":\"Specify local save and recovery protocol\",\"domain\":\"persistence\",\"targets\":[\"shared\",\"web\",\"pwa\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"REQ-0006\",\"REQ-0012\",\"NFR-0002\",\"NFR-0003\",\"NFR-0005\"],\"bounded_outcome\":\"A schema protocol specifies immutable revisions, checksums, current-pointer validation, known-good retention, quarantine, separate preferences, deletion confirmation, and safe-boundary persistence rules.\",\"prerequisites\":[\"IMP-0002\",\"IMP-0004\",\"IMP-0003\"],\"ownership\":{\"files\":[\"src/core/save/{schema,compatibility,migrations}/\",\"src/platform/web/persistence/\",\"tests/{core,platform}/save*\",\"docs/save-and-recovery.md\"],\"data\":[\"save snapshot and preference schemas\",\"quarantine record\"],\"api\":[\"snapshot repository and recovery protocol\"]},\"forbidden_scope\":[\"cloud sync\",\"identity\",\"PWA cache records\",\"eviction guarantee\"],\"verification\":\"Fault fixtures cover interrupted write, checksum failure, malformed data, quota/permission failure, quarantine, retry, and selected-slot deletion.\",\"human_external_gate\":\"GATE-0003 / DEC-0003 storage API, quota, support window, and recovery policy.\",\"complexity\":\"high\",\"status\":\"gated\"},\n+    {\"id\":\"IMP-0007\",\"title\":\"Define pure save migration runner\",\"domain\":\"persistence\",\"targets\":[\"shared\",\"web\",\"pwa\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"REQ-0006\",\"NFR-0002\",\"NFR-0003\"],\"bounded_outcome\":\"Ordered, pure migrations declare supported versions and promote only validated candidates while preserving original invalid bytes for quarantine.\",\"prerequisites\":[\"IMP-0005\",\"IMP-0006\"],\"ownership\":{\"files\":[\"src/core/save/{migrations,compatibility}/\",\"tests/core/save/fixtures\"],\"data\":[\"migration registry and predecessor fixtures\"],\"api\":[\"migration runner API\"]},\"forbidden_scope\":[\"storage driver changes\",\"future data export\",\"automatic destructive repair\"],\"verification\":\"Every declared predecessor migrates once; unsupported or failed migration leaves the original candidate intact and quarantined.\",\"human_external_gate\":\"GATE-0003 / DEC-0003 support-window approval.\",\"complexity\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"gated\"},\n+    {\"id\":\"IMP-0008\",\"title\":\"Bound P0 identity, authorization, and connected-service exclusions\",\"domain\":\"security\",\"targets\":[\"shared\",\"web\",\"pwa\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"REQ-0013\",\"REQ-0014\",\"REQ-0015\",\"NFR-0012\"],\"bounded_outcome\":\"Architecture and negative contract tests demonstrate that local campaign start/save/resume require no account identifier, token, remote profile, role, entitlement, multiplayer, or safety service.\",\"prerequisites\":[\"IMP-0002\",\"IMP-0004\"],\"ownership\":{\"files\":[\"docs/security-boundary.md\",\"tests/core/connected-scope-exclusion.*\"],\"data\":[\"future connected-service approval checklist\"],\"api\":[\"local-slot identity contract\"]},\"forbidden_scope\":[\"sign-in\",\"OAuth\",\"sync\",\"roles\",\"moderation\",\"purchases\",\"server APIs\"],\"verification\":\"Static scan and negative fixtures find no identity/token/privilege fields or network client in P0 foundation modules.\",\"human_external_gate\":\"GATE-0006 / DEC-0006 before any connected implementation.\",\"complexity\":\"low\",\"status\":\"current\"},\n+    {\"id\":\"IMP-0009\",\"title\":\"Define privacy-safe local diagnostics boundary\",\"domain\":\"privacy\",\"targets\":[\"web\",\"pwa\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"REQ-0012\",\"NFR-0006\"],\"bounded_outcome\":\"A bounded local diagnostic schema, consent and clear controls, redaction rules, and no-network guardrails support future player recovery without collecting save or dialogue payloads.\",\"prerequisites\":[\"IMP-0002\",\"IMP-0003\",\"IMP-0006\"],\"ownership\":{\"files\":[\"src/platform/web/diagnostics/\",\"src/app/recovery/diagnostic-contract.*\",\"tests/platform/diagnostics.*\",\"docs/privacy-and-recovery.md\"],\"data\":[\"redacted local diagnostic record\",\"consent state\"],\"api\":[\"diagnostic recorder interface\"]},\"forbidden_scope\":[\"diagnostic provider/transport\",\"remote analytics\",\"retention promise\",\"secrets\"],\"verification\":\"Tests prove diagnostics are absent without consent, redact payloads, and can be deleted locally.\",\"human_external_gate\":\"GATE-0005 / DEC-0005 before transport, retention, hosting, or support claims.\",\"complexity\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"gated\"},\n+    {\"id\":\"IMP-0010\",\"title\":\"Establish semantic accessibility design tokens\",\"domain\":\"accessibility\",\"targets\":[\"shared\",\"web\",\"pwa\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"REQ-0007\",\"REQ-0010\",\"NFR-0004\",\"NFR-0008\"],\"bounded_outcome\":\"Original semantic tokens cover typography, spacing, focus, motion, touch targets, status, contrast, and non-colour cues, enabling later responsive web UI and inherited PWA UI.\",\"prerequisites\":[\"IMP-0001\",\"IMP-0002\"],\"ownership\":{\"files\":[\"src/app/design/tokens/\",\"docs/design-tokens.md\",\"tests/app/design-tokens.*\"],\"data\":[\"semantic token inventory\"],\"api\":[\"token consumption contract\"]},\"forbidden_scope\":[\"screens\",\"maps\",\"final artwork/fonts\",\"final breakpoints\",\"copied reference styling\"],\"verification\":\"Token validation proves semantic labels/non-colour cues and reduced-motion values in representative fixtures.\",\"human_external_gate\":\"GATE-0002 and GATE-0004 before numeric contrast/font/breakpoint claims.\",\"complexity\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"gated\"},\n+    {\"id\":\"IMP-0011\",\"title\":\"Create original-content provenance control\",\"domain\":\"content\",\"targets\":[\"shared\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"REQ-0001\",\"REQ-0008\",\"NFR-0008\"],\"bounded_outcome\":\"A provenance record format, review checklist, and source-asset manifest make authorship and permitted functional reference scope auditable before authored content enters a build.\",\"prerequisites\":[\"IMP-0005\"],\"ownership\":{\"files\":[\"assets/source-manifest.*\",\"docs/original-content-review.md\",\"tests/content/provenance.*\"],\"data\":[\"provenance manifest and review disposition\"],\"api\":[\"provenance validator input contract\"]},\"forbidden_scope\":[\"creating art/audio/story\",\"licensing approval\",\"automatic legal clearance\"],\"verification\":\"Validator rejects missing provenance fields; human creative review is recorded for each authored package.\",\"human_external_gate\":\"Human creative/provenance review; legal or licensing review if applicable under GATE-0007.\",\"complexity\":\"low\",\"status\":\"current\"},\n+    {\"id\":\"IMP-0012\",\"title\":\"Document foundation architecture and recovery boundaries\",\"domain\":\"documentation\",\"targets\":[\"shared\",\"web\",\"pwa\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"NFR-0012\",\"NFR-0010\",\"NFR-0002\",\"NFR-0003\"],\"bounded_outcome\":\"Developer documentation records ownership, command flow, save-versus-cache separation, deferred connected scope, and the decisions/gates that later domain authors must preserve.\",\"prerequisites\":[\"IMP-0002\",\"IMP-0004\",\"IMP-0006\",\"IMP-0008\"],\"ownership\":{\"files\":[\"docs/{architecture,development,save-and-recovery,security-boundary}.md\"],\"data\":[\"foundation decision and ownership index\"],\"api\":[\"documented public-boundary inventory\"]},\"forbidden_scope\":[\"player release guide\",\"operational rollout\",\"claiming approved vendor or policy choices\"],\"verification\":\"Documentation review cross-checks every foundation contract's ownership, dependency, and gate against this catalogue.\",\"human_external_gate\":\"None; approval gates are documented, not resolved.\",\"complexity\":\"low\",\"status\":\"current\"}\n+  ],\n+  \"expansion_queue\": [\n+    {\"id\":\"SHARD-02\",\"title\":\"Campaign content and domain logic\",\"max_contracts\":250,\"depends_on\":[\"SHARD-01\"],\"covers\":[\"exploration\",\"dialogue\",\"quests\",\"tutorial\",\"combat\",\"inventory\",\"party progression\",\"town/dungeon/ending content\",\"content validation\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"REQ-0001\",\"REQ-0002\",\"REQ-0003\",\"REQ-0004\",\"REQ-0005\",\"REQ-0008\",\"NFR-0007\",\"NFR-0008\"],\"gate\":\"GATE-0004\",\"target_allocation\":\"shared core and content only; no UI ownership\",\"state\":\"queued\"},\n+    {\"id\":\"SHARD-03\",\"title\":\"Session, UI, input, and accessibility\",\"max_contracts\":250,\"depends_on\":[\"SHARD-01\",\"SHARD-02\"],\"covers\":[\"session/checkpoints\",\"semantic responsive shell\",\"game panels\",\"keyboard/mouse/touch/gamepad adapters\",\"settings\",\"localisation\",\"captions\",\"feedback\",\"error recovery UI\",\"accessibility tests\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"REQ-0005\",\"REQ-0006\",\"REQ-0007\",\"REQ-0009\",\"REQ-0010\",\"REQ-0012\",\"NFR-0002\",\"NFR-0003\",\"NFR-0004\",\"NFR-0005\"],\"gate\":\"GATE-0002,GATE-0003,GATE-0004\",\"target_allocation\":\"shared UI model; web input/layout adapter; PWA inherits UI with no separate UI fork\",\"state\":\"queued\"},\n+    {\"id\":\"SHARD-04\",\"title\":\"PWA delivery, performance, operations, and release evidence\",\"max_contracts\":250,\"depends_on\":[\"SHARD-01\",\"SHARD-02\",\"SHARD-03\"],\"covers\":[\"PWA manifest/install\",\"service-worker cache lifecycle\",\"offline/update recovery\",\"performance measurement\",\"security headers\",\"release checks\",\"observability\",\"quality automation\",\"player/operator documentation\",\"platform certification assessment\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"REQ-0011\",\"REQ-0012\",\"NFR-0001\",\"NFR-0003\",\"NFR-0006\",\"NFR-0009\",\"NFR-0011\",\"NFR-0012\"],\"gate\":\"GATE-0002,GATE-0005,GATE-0007\",\"target_allocation\":\"web release build and PWA service-worker/install adapter are distinct; shared core owns neither cache nor hosting\",\"state\":\"queued\"},\n+    {\"id\":\"SHARD-05\",\"title\":\"Connected-scope decision package\",\"max_contracts\":250,\"depends_on\":[\"SHARD-01\"],\"covers\":[\"identity/sync conflict policy\",\"multiplayer/player safety\",\"live operations\",\"commerce/entitlements\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"REQ-0014\",\"REQ-0015\"],\"gate\":\"GATE-0006\",\"target_allocation\":\"no P0 target implementation; research/decision outputs only if explicitly authorised\",\"state\":\"hold\"}\n+  ],\n+  \"requirement_coverage\": {\n+    \"REQ-0001\":\"queued: SHARD-02; provenance foundation IMP-0011\",\"REQ-0002\":\"queued: SHARD-02\",\"REQ-0003\":\"queued: SHARD-02\",\"REQ-0004\":\"queued: SHARD-02\",\"REQ-0005\":\"queued: SHARD-02 and SHARD-03\",\"REQ-0006\":\"current/gated: IMP-0006, IMP-0007; queued: SHARD-03\",\"REQ-0007\":\"current/gated: IMP-0010; queued: SHARD-03\",\"REQ-0008\":\"current: IMP-0005, IMP-0011; queued: SHARD-02\",\"REQ-0009\":\"queued: SHARD-03\",\"REQ-0010\":\"current/gated: IMP-0010; queued: SHARD-03\",\"REQ-0011\":\"queued: SHARD-04\",\"REQ-0012\":\"current/gated: IMP-0006, IMP-0009; queued: SHARD-03 and SHARD-04\",\"REQ-0013\":\"current: IMP-0002, IMP-0008\",\"REQ-0014\":\"gated: SHARD-05 / GATE-0006; no P0 implementation\",\"REQ-0015\":\"hold: SHARD-05 / GATE-0006; no P0 implementation\",\"NFR-0001\":\"queued: SHARD-04\",\"NFR-0002\":\"current/gated: IMP-0004, IMP-0006, IMP-0007\",\"NFR-0003\":\"current/gated: IMP-0006, IMP-0007; queued: SHARD-04\",\"NFR-0004\":\"current/gated: IMP-0010; queued: SHARD-03\",\"NFR-0005\":\"current/gated: IMP-0006; queued: SHARD-03\",\"NFR-0006\":\"current/gated: IMP-0009; queued: SHARD-04\",\"NFR-0007\":\"current: IMP-0005; queued: SHARD-02\",\"NFR-0008\":\"current: IMP-0005, IMP-0010, IMP-0011; queued: SHARD-02\",\"NFR-0009\":\"gated: SHARD-04 / GATE-0002\",\"NFR-0010\":\"current: IMP-0001, IMP-0002, IMP-0003, IMP-0004; queued target adapters in SHARD-03 and SHARD-04\",\"NFR-0011\":\"gated: SHARD-04 / GATE-0005\",\"NFR-0012\":\"current/gated: IMP-0001, IMP-0002, IMP-0003, IMP-0008, IMP-0012; queued: SHARD-04\"\n+  },\n+  \"dependency_graph\": {\"nodes\":[\"IMP-0001\",\"IMP-0002\",\"IMP-0003\",\"IMP-0004\",\"IMP-0005\",\"IMP-0006\",\"IMP-0007\",\"IMP-0008\",\"IMP-0009\",\"IMP-0010\",\"IMP-0011\",\"IMP-0012\"],\"acyclic\":true,\"validation\":\"Each prerequisite points only to an earlier numbered contract; SHARD dependencies only point from later shards to earlier shards.\"}\n+}\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..2611068b5330aa12eb273cf04221787b84bc0a54\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,68 @@\n+# Implementation catalogue index\n+\n+This is the F012 implementation-authoring index for **mock-fantasy-quest-4**.\n+The machine-readable source is\n+[`implementation-catalogue-index.json`](implementation-catalogue-index.json).\n+It decomposes only the first bounded shard; it does not author R-series\n+runbooks or approve any decision gate.\n+\n+## Scope and ownership rules\n+\n+- **SHARD-01 \u2014 Foundation and core contracts** contains 12 independently\n+  verifiable contracts (limit: 250). It establishes framework-neutral seams,\n+  deterministic data contracts, local persistence/recovery protocols, quality\n+  controls, and documentation. It does not implement campaign behaviour,\n+  player UI, PWA lifecycle, or release actions.\n+- **Shared** owns campaign rules and platform-neutral contracts. **Web** owns\n+  browser input, responsive layout, origin storage, and web builds. **PWA** is\n+  a delivery/cache/install adaptation only: it reuses the shared game and web\n+  UI, while owning its service-worker lifecycle. Save data and cache data are\n+  deliberately separate.\n+- `GATE-*` records block dependent authoring; they are not defaults. The\n+  catalogue keeps connected capabilities out of P0 under `GATE-0006`.\n+- Content must be original. The functional reference never authorises copied\n+  names, text, lore, art, maps, layouts, music, or interaction choreography.\n+\n+## Current contracts\n+\n+| ID | Domain | Outcome | Prerequisites | Gate/status |\n+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n+| IMP-0001 | Foundation | Reproducible shared project baseline | \u2014 | GATE-0001 / gated |\n+| IMP-0002 | Foundation | Core and adapter dependency seams | IMP-0001 | current |\n+| IMP-0003 | Tests | Deterministic test/fixture harness | IMP-0001\u20130002 | current |\n+| IMP-0004 | Data | Deterministic state/command/event contract | IMP-0002\u20130003 | current |\n+| IMP-0005 | Content | Versioned content schema and validator | IMP-0001, 0003\u20130004 | current |\n+| IMP-0006 | Persistence | Local save/recovery protocol | IMP-0002\u20130004 | GATE-0003 / gated |\n+| IMP-0007 | Persistence | Pure migration runner | IMP-0005\u20130006 | GATE-0003 / gated |\n+| IMP-0008 | Security | P0 connected-service exclusions | IMP-0002, 0004 | current |\n+| IMP-0009 | Privacy | Local, redacted diagnostics boundary | IMP-0002\u20130003, 0006 | GATE-0005 / gated |\n+| IMP-0010 | Accessibility | Semantic design-token contract | IMP-0001\u20130002 | GATE-0002/0004 / gated |\n+| IMP-0011 | Content | Original-content provenance control | IMP-0005 | current + human review |\n+| IMP-0012 | Documentation | Foundation boundary documentation | IMP-0002, 0004, 0006, 0008 | current |\n+\n+Each JSON contract has one title, domain, target allocation, requirement IDs,\n+bounded outcome, prerequisite list, sole files/data/API ownership, forbidden\n+scope, verification, human/external gate, complexity, and status. The only\n+dependency direction is toward earlier contracts, so the current graph is\n+acyclic.\n+\n+## Domain-expansion queue\n+\n+| Queue ID | Bounded domain (maximum contracts) | Dependency | Requirements/gate | Allocation |\n+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n+| SHARD-02 | Campaign content and domain logic (250) | SHARD-01 | Core P0 campaign; GATE-0004 | Shared core/content; no UI |\n+| SHARD-03 | Session, UI, input, and accessibility (250) | SHARD-01\u201302 | REQ-0005\u20130007, 0009\u20130010, 0012; GATE-0002\u20130004 | Shared UI model, Web adapters, inherited PWA UI |\n+| SHARD-04 | PWA delivery, performance, operations, and release evidence (250) | SHARD-01\u201303 | REQ-0011\u20130012, NFR-0001/0003/0006/0009/0011/0012; GATE-0002/0005/0007 | Separate web build and PWA lifecycle |\n+| SHARD-05 | Connected-scope decision package (250) | SHARD-01 | REQ-0014\u20130015; GATE-0006 | Hold; research/decision outputs only if authorised |\n+\n+The JSON `requirement_coverage` map accounts for every canonical `REQ-*` and\n+`NFR-*` as current, queued, gated, or held, naming the corresponding contract\n+or expansion shard. No requirement is silently rejected or deferred.\n+\n+## Structural validation\n+\n+Use this check after edits:\n+\n+```sh\n+node -e 'const c=require(\"./projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json\"); const ids=new Set(c.contracts.map(x=>x.id)); if (ids.size!==c.contracts.length || c.first_bounded_domain.contract_count>c.first_bounded_domain.contract_limit || c.expansion_queue.some(x=>x.max_contracts>250) || Object.keys(c.requirement_coverage).length!==27 || c.contracts.some(x=>x.prerequisites.some(p=>!ids.has(p)))) process.exit(1); console.log(\"catalogue structural check passed\")'\n+```\n\nhook: PostToolUse\nhook: PostToolUse Failed\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..7f4cf1bcf472afd1c38d8fac9f5522e6a6b41be2\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json\n@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@\n+{\n+  \"catalogue_id\": \"mock-fantasy-quest-4-implementation-catalogue\",\n+  \"version\": 1,\n+  \"source\": [\"../specification/README.md\", \"../specification/requirements.json\", \"05-delivery-map.md\", \"06-foundation-domain-contracts.md\", \"07-feature-experience-contracts.md\", \"08-quality-operations-contracts.md\"],\n+  \"scope\": \"P0 is an original, offline-capable 2D single-player fantasy RPG delivered through a shared web core and a PWA delivery adaptation. Connected services are not P0 implementation scope.\",\n+  \"first_bounded_domain\": {\"id\": \"SHARD-01\", \"title\": \"Foundation and core contracts\", \"contract_limit\": 250, \"contract_count\": 12, \"state\": \"ready_for_authoring\", \"boundary\": \"Framework-neutral seams, deterministic state/data contracts, local persistence protocol, quality foundations, and original-design controls; excludes campaign rules, UI flows, PWA lifecycle, and release execution.\"},\n+  \"contracts\": [\n+    {\"id\":\"IMP-0001\",\"title\":\"Bootstrap reproducible shared project baseline\",\"domain\":\"foundation\",\"targets\":[\"shared\",\"web\",\"pwa\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"NFR-0010\",\"NFR-0012\"],\"bounded_outcome\":\"A framework-neutral project skeleton documents one bootstrap, lint, format, and deterministic test command with isolated shared, web-adapter, PWA-adapter, content, and test directories.\",\"prerequisites\":[],\"ownership\":{\"files\":[\"root build/tooling configuration\",\"src/{core,content,app,platform/web,platform/pwa}/\",\"tests/\",\"docs/development.md\"],\"data\":[\"pinned toolchain declaration\"],\"api\":[\"build/test command interface\"]},\"forbidden_scope\":[\"selecting framework/package manager/CI without DEC-0001\",\"gameplay\",\"service worker\",\"hosting\"],\"verification\":\"Clean approved-runtime checkout runs the documented deterministic sample test, lint, and format checks.\",\"human_external_gate\":\"GATE-0001 / DEC-0001 framework, package-manager, and CI selection before implementation.\",\"complexity\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"gated\"},\n+    {\"id\":\"IMP-0002\",\"title\":\"Enforce shared-core and adapter dependency seams\",\"domain\":\"foundation\",\"targets\":[\"shared\",\"web\",\"pwa\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"NFR-0010\",\"REQ-0013\",\"NFR-0012\"],\"bounded_outcome\":\"A dependency policy and public interfaces prevent core code from importing browser, renderer, clock, network, or platform modules; adapters submit commands and render returned state/events.\",\"prerequisites\":[\"IMP-0001\"],\"ownership\":{\"files\":[\"src/core/public interfaces\",\"src/platform/{web,pwa}/adapter interfaces\",\"architecture dependency rules\",\"docs/architecture.md\"],\"data\":[\"dependency-policy manifest\"],\"api\":[\"Command, state, event, and adapter interfaces\"]},\"forbidden_scope\":[\"concrete combat/exploration/UI\",\"account or network client\",\"target-specific campaign rules\"],\"verification\":\"A dependency-rule test rejects forbidden core imports and a fixture adapter proves command-only interaction.\",\"human_external_gate\":\"None; retain GATE-0001 for tool-specific enforcement.\",\"complexity\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"current\"},\n+    {\"id\":\"IMP-0003\",\"title\":\"Create deterministic test and fixture harness\",\"domain\":\"tests\",\"targets\":[\"shared\",\"web\",\"pwa\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"NFR-0010\",\"NFR-0012\"],\"bounded_outcome\":\"Layered unit, content, integration, and reserved browser-test conventions provide isolated RNG/clock and persistence fixtures with no real service or player data access.\",\"prerequisites\":[\"IMP-0001\",\"IMP-0002\"],\"ownership\":{\"files\":[\"test-runner configuration\",\"tests/{core,content,platform,app}/fixtures\",\"docs/testing.md\"],\"data\":[\"deterministic fixture factories\"],\"api\":[\"test fixture and fake clock/RNG interfaces\"]},\"forbidden_scope\":[\"final feature assertions\",\"real browser/device matrix claims\",\"production telemetry\"],\"verification\":\"Repeated core fixture execution has identical results; a deliberately failing fixture is detected; fixture storage is isolated.\",\"human_external_gate\":\"GATE-0002 before compatibility or performance claims.\",\"complexity\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"current\"},\n+    {\"id\":\"IMP-0004\",\"title\":\"Define deterministic campaign state and command contract\",\"domain\":\"data\",\"targets\":[\"shared\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"REQ-0001\",\"REQ-0003\",\"REQ-0004\",\"REQ-0006\",\"NFR-0002\",\"NFR-0010\"],\"bounded_outcome\":\"Immutable versioned state, command/result/event envelopes, revision and interaction identifiers, deterministic RNG state, and invariant helpers define legal transition mechanics without feature state machines.\",\"prerequisites\":[\"IMP-0002\",\"IMP-0003\"],\"ownership\":{\"files\":[\"src/core/{state,commands,events,invariants,rng}/\",\"tests/core/contract.*\"],\"data\":[\"campaign snapshot envelope\",\"deterministic RNG state\"],\"api\":[\"Core command/state/event API\"]},\"forbidden_scope\":[\"authored values\",\"combat/inventory/quest algorithms\",\"save driver\",\"UI selection state\",\"account/network state\"],\"verification\":\"Invalid and stale commands do not mutate state; duplicate interaction IDs cause no extra durable transition.\",\"human_external_gate\":\"GATE-0004 before concrete party/content shapes.\",\"complexity\":\"high\",\"status\":\"current\"},\n+    {\"id\":\"IMP-0005\",\"title\":\"Define versioned content schema and validation boundary\",\"domain\":\"content\",\"targets\":[\"shared\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"REQ-0002\",\"REQ-0008\",\"NFR-0007\",\"NFR-0008\"],\"bounded_outcome\":\"Typed content-package schema and validator cover IDs, references, locale keys, assets, predicates, rewards, and reachability but contain no authored campaign expression.\",\"prerequisites\":[\"IMP-0001\",\"IMP-0004\",\"IMP-0003\"],\"ownership\":{\"files\":[\"src/content/{schema,validator,registry}/\",\"tests/content/validation.*\",\"docs/content-authoring.md\"],\"data\":[\"versioned content package format\",\"asset/provenance manifest schema\"],\"api\":[\"content registry and validator API\"]},\"forbidden_scope\":[\"town/dungeon dialogue/maps/assets\",\"copied reference expression\",\"release packaging\"],\"verification\":\"Valid minimum package passes; each invalid reference class fails; a graph fixture checks opening-to-ending reachability.\",\"human_external_gate\":\"GATE-0004 for quantities, locale, and content detail; human provenance review remains required.\",\"complexity\":\"high\",\"status\":\"current\"},\n+    {\"i